      "writtenOn": "2024-02-22T20:48:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This file declares a _lot_ of top level names without introducing a namespace or beginning the names with `Sk`. This is unfriendly to our users. Particularly a top-level `StableKey`--I wouldn\u0027t be surprised if this were a real-world conflict somewhere. \n\nA namespace is probably best, but `Sk` prefixes would also work.\n\nOr... maybe SkRuntimeEffect can house them all as public??",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "8cc9c48c8370adda5dfc165a8af93732d652446b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4a297e41_8883d601",
